{"name":"Retreat","hex":"#7a8076","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Retreat","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A locality in the Tamworth council area, north eastern New South Wales, Australia.","A locality in George Town council area and the City of Launceston, northern Tasmania, Australia."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Retreat"}],"entries":[{"title":"Withdrawal (military)","blocks":[{"text":"A tactical withdrawal or retreating defensive action is a type of military operation, generally meaning that retreating forces draw back while maintaining contact with the enemy. A withdrawal may be undertaken as part of a general retreat, to consolidate forces, to occupy ground that is more easily defended, force the enemy to overextend to secure a decisive victory, or to lead the enemy into an ambush. It is considered a relatively risky operation, requiring discipline to keep from turning into a disorganized rout or at the very least doing severe damage to the military's morale."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Napoleons_retreat_from_Moscow_by_Adolph_Northen.jpg/330px-Napoleons_retreat_from_Moscow_by_Adolph_Northen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Withdrawal_(military)"},{"title":"Retreat (survivalism)","blocks":[{"text":"In the survivalist subculture or movement, a retreat is a place of refuge. Sometimes their retreats are called a bug-out location (BOL), a bunker, or a bolt hole. Survivalist retreats are intended to be self-sufficient and easily defended. Generally, they are located in sparsely populated outback rural areas."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Fort_Furggels_-_Bunker_North.jpg/330px-Fort_Furggels_-_Bunker_North.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Retreat_(survivalism)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Gari-Melchers-War-Highsmith.jpeg/500px-Gari-Melchers-War-Highsmith.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Gari-Melchers-War-Highsmith.jpeg/1280px-Gari-Melchers-War-Highsmith.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Gari-Melchers-War-Highsmith.jpeg/500px-Gari-Melchers-War-Highsmith.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGari-Melchers-War-Highsmith.jpeg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Napoleons_retreat_from_Moscow_by_Adolph_Northen.jpg/500px-Napoleons_retreat_from_Moscow_by_Adolph_Northen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Napoleons_retreat_from_Moscow_by_Adolph_Northen.jpg/500px-Napoleons_retreat_from_Moscow_by_Adolph_Northen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Napoleon's withdrawal from Moscow","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANapoleons_retreat_from_Moscow_by_Adolph_Northen.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/National_Museum_in_Poznan_-_Przej%C5%9Bcie_przez_Berezyn%C4%99.JPG/500px-National_Museum_in_Poznan_-_Przej%C5%9Bcie_przez_Berezyn%C4%99.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/National_Museum_in_Poznan_-_Przej%C5%9Bcie_przez_Berezyn%C4%99.JPG/1280px-National_Museum_in_Poznan_-_Przej%C5%9Bcie_przez_Berezyn%C4%99.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/National_Museum_in_Poznan_-_P